### Expected behaviour

SGW-C should not crash when the associated S11 transaction is missing.
If s11_xact cannot be found, SGW-C should:
safely reject / ignore the response

### Observed Behaviour

SGW-C aborts due to assertion failure in S5-C handler.

### eNodeB/gNodeB

No

### UE Models and versions

No

### Open5GS Release, Revision, or Tag

v2.7.6

### Description
SGW-C can be forced to abort (core dump) due to an ogs_assert in the PFCP path when processing a crafted GTPv2-C session setup flow. The crash is triggered after SGW-C enters session context, then hits an error path (No GTP TEID) and finally aborts on: Assert: ogs_pfcp_build_update_far_activate: Assertion 'far->apply_action & OGS_PFCP_APPLY_ACTION_FORW' failed Location: ../lib/pfcp/build.c:647, which results in DoS. 

