### Expected behaviour

SGW-C should handle stale bearer references gracefully:
If bearer lookup fails, return an error / drop safely, without crashing.


### Observed Behaviour

A crafted DeleteBearerResponse causes ogs_assert(bearer) after bearer lookup returns NULL, terminating SGW-C (DoS).

### eNodeB/gNodeB

No

### UE Models and versions

No

### Open5GS Release, Revision, or Tag

v2.7.6

### Steps to reproduce

### Description
SGW-C can be crashed by sending a delayed GTPv2-C Downlink Data Notification Ack (DDN Ack) on S11 after the related bearer has been removed.

1. Start a new go project inside a new folder: `go mod init poc`
2. Create a `main.go` and paste the code below:
