### Expected behaviour

SGW-C should handle lateDDN Ack safely:
If the bearer is already removed, SGW-C should drop the DDN Ack or return an appropriate error (if any), and log a warning.
It should not hit ogs_assert().

### Observed Behaviour

When DDN Ack arrives after DeleteSession has removed the bearer, SGW-C enters sgwc_s11_handle_downlink_data_notification_ack and triggers ogs_assert(bearer) (bearer is NULL/stale), causing immediate process abort and control-plane DoS.

